    {
      "id": "0bqhZg7lR9-QMzU7hBsu6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1242.8456175062393,
      "y": 433.16666666666674,
      "width": 213.4198760986328,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2087647459,
      "version": 316,
      "versionNonce": 746198579,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795401382011,
      "created": 1795322895906,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"Two pointers moving\ntoward each other, or\nboth going the same\nway.\"",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "wk_GNenhVwZrcd1djO-vw",
      "originalText": "\"Two pointers moving toward each other, or both going the same way.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mOHgiRfQZySB2wFXVOWtD",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1136.777777777778,
      "y": 718.7777777777778,
      "width": 446.66666666666674,
      "height": 240.55555555555543,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aM",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1708336317,
      "version": 290,
      "versionNonce": 1436097553,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "u-b-EnNRmqbrKEKlh7EZM"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1795570558817,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "u-b-EnNRmqbrKEKlh7EZM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1146.4412502712676,
      "y": 726.5555555555555,
      "width": 427.3397216796875,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1638451165,
      "version": 231,
      "versionNonce": 891122161,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795570558817,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "you use two positions in the data to avoid\nchecking every pair, so you turn an O(n²)\nscan into O(n). Opposite ends is for sorted\ndata or palindromes, where comparing the\ntwo ends tells you which side to move\ninward. Same direction is fast and slow,\nwhere one pointer reads ahead and the\nother writes or tracks, like removing\nduplicates in place.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "mOHgiRfQZySB2wFXVOWtD",
      "originalText": "you use two positions in the data to avoid checking every pair, so you turn an O(n²) scan into O(n). Opposite ends is for sorted data or palindromes, where comparing the two ends tells you which side to move inward. Same direction is fast and slow, where one pointer reads ahead and the other writes or tracks, like removing duplicates in place.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xKHyK17uXAiesakNa2UAF",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1183.4444444444448,
      "y": 548.7777777777778,
      "width": 323.33333333333337,
      "height": 160,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aO",
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 1139262769,
      "version": 224,
      "versionNonce": 1460221681,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "wrqqr7gnf2NxStzhBQ0Ms"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1795570556815,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wrqqr7gnf2NxStzhBQ0Ms",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1189.7212185329865,
      "y": 553.7777777777778,
      "width": 310.77978515625,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aOV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 775656785,
      "version": 170,
      "versionNonce": 193409233,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795570556815,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Two pointers means you keep\ntwo positions in your data, so\nyou don't have to check every\npossible pair. That turns a slow\nscan into one pass.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "xKHyK17uXAiesakNa2UAF",
      "originalText": "Two pointers means you keep two positions in your data, so you don't have to check every possible pair. That turns a slow scan into one pass.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
